{"title":"Ceramic Engineer Roadmap","role":"Ceramic Engineer","summary":"A Ceramic Engineer develops, processes, characterises and improves ceramic and advanced ceramic materials. The field covers traditional ceramics such as tiles, sanitaryware, glass-related materials and refractories, as well as advanced ceramics used in electronics, aerospace, energy, biomedical devices, semiconductor manufacturing and high-temperature applications.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment. Ceramic Engineering is a highly specialised undergraduate route for ceramic-materials careers."}],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Current degree"},{"text":"B.Tech / B.E. Ceramic Engineering"}],[{"text":"Desired career"},{"text":"Ceramic Engineer"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Engineering & Technology"}],[{"text":"Primary route"},{"text":"Ceramic Engineering → Materials/Ceramic Industry → Specialist/Technical Leadership"}],[{"text":"Core domains"},{"text":"Ceramic processing, materials science, powder technology, sintering, characterization, refractory technology"}],[{"text":"Major industries"},{"text":"Advanced ceramics, refractories, tiles, sanitaryware, glass, cement, electronics, aerospace, energy, biomedical"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Ceramic-processing fundamentals, laboratory skills, materials characterisation and industrial internships"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in advanced ceramics, refractories, electronic ceramics, production, quality or R&D"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Ceramic/Materials Engineer, Process Engineer, R&D Engineer or Technical Specialist"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine ceramic expertise with advanced materials, additive manufacturing, automation, AI and sustainable processing"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are career-planning horizons rather than guaranteed promotion timelines."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, physics, chemistry, programming and drawing"},{"text":"University + NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Technical calculations and Python/Excel exercises"},{"text":"Engineering foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Materials science, crystallography and mineral fundamentals"},{"text":"Materials/ceramics coursework"},{"text":"Crystal-structure and materials reports"},{"text":"Materials foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Ceramic raw materials, powders and ceramic chemistry"},{"text":"Core ceramic courses"},{"text":"Raw-material characterisation project"},{"text":"Ceramic-material understanding"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Forming, drying, firing and sintering"},{"text":"Laboratory + NPTEL"},{"text":"Ceramic-processing experiment"},{"text":"Processing capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Phase diagrams, refractory materials and advanced ceramics"},{"text":"Materials courses + lab work"},{"text":"Phase-diagram/material-selection project"},{"text":"Materials engineering"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Characterisation, quality control and industrial production"},{"text":"Laboratory + industry exposure"},{"text":"XRD/SEM/thermal-analysis report"},{"text":"Industrial readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced ceramics, process optimisation and automation"},{"text":"Advanced courses + industry"},{"text":"Process optimisation project"},{"text":"Specialist capability"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Industry internship/capstone + placement preparation"},{"text":"I